{"title":"2005 IMO Shortlist Problems/N3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/N3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Mongolia</i>)\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> be positive integers.  Suppose that the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5b0b2eee14fa5174864e17b553c6af157a9d3b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = a+b+c+d+e+f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"201\" height=\"16\" /> divides both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/b/f6b4d2de85df0746d2804d0f98d0c41125eec74f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc + def$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/b/19bdc7e53de2d90998463c2697accef001a1671e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+bc+ca - de-ef-fd$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"219\" height=\"16\" />.  Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is composite.\n</p><p><i>This was also Problem 1 of the 2nd 2006 German TST, and a problem at the 2006 Indian IMO Training Camp.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/N3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b5a07f2a22fcb2626031da734012c71b549782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle x$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> we have\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f500fc22d20c9b29cbd1fda02f3c88eddbf2fadf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+a)(x+b)(x+c) \\equiv x^3 + (a+b+c)x^2 + (ab+bc+ca)x + abc \\equiv x^3 - (d+e+f)x^2 + (de+ef+fd)x - def$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"890\" height=\"19\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/1/c41d7836a2858223508378a1e94c01610acfeb78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\equiv (x-d)(x-e)(x-f) \\pmod{S}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"262\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>since each coefficient of the first two polynomials is congruent to the corresponding coefficient of the second two polynomials, mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d152214fba74c1f8a12f3d44452016018239bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle S$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />.  Now, suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d152214fba74c1f8a12f3d44452016018239bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle S$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> is prime.  Since\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/8/338867bab06dc3704819f441c7c78c1b66b857c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(d+a)(d+b)(d+c) \\equiv (d-d)(d-e)(d-f) \\equiv 0 \\pmod{S}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"460\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c534aa10b129f45493b841ca9919489fc0111e6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle d+a, d+b, d+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"136\" height=\"16\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d152214fba74c1f8a12f3d44452016018239bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle S$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />, say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/8/0b8a8cf2c5cbbb247d4ca94ce04ea2961ccd8278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle d+a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/625a6152a6e8465c61732ea58ed3637c381e1219.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle d,a &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />, this means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/e/e1e3d396360c2b9d326a658e16e01233629a224c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d+a \\ge S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />.  But since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/1/5518a8c7df303493e0bc3002973797a293cc60dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, \\ldots, f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> are positive integers, we then have\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2a497e3c9c921e3faeced16fe11d5e74817688c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S &gt; d+a \\ge S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"17\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>a contradiction.  <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Halmos&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:Halmos (page does not exist)\">Template:Halmos</a>\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/N3&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/N3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Shortlist_Problems\" title=\"2005 IMO Shortlist Problems\">2005 IMO Shortlist Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Germany_TST_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 Germany TST Problems (page does not exist)\">2006 Germany TST Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMOTC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 IMOTC Problems (page does not exist)\">2006 IMOTC Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=525979#525979\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017190236\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.034 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 133/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 373/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4209/5000000 bytes\n-->\